+# Security Review: STORY-322 — Loader Health Dashboard
+
+**Review Date:** 2026-05-03
+**Reviewer:** Phase 6b Security Review Agent
+**Story Scope:** Small
+**Verdict:** PASS
+
+---
+
+## 1. Summary
+
+STORY-322 adds a read-only "Loaders" dashboard page that consumes existing `/healthz` data and provides a "Reset Circuit" action via `POST /api/loaders/{name}/reset-circuit`. The security posture is strong: no new backend endpoints beyond the existing reset-circuit route, no new authentication mechanisms, no database migrations, and full `PermissionGuard` admin-role gating on the page. The only write action (circuit reset) requires a mandatory `reason` field and is restricted to admin users.
+
+---
+
+## 2. External API Isolation (REQUIRED by Project Policy)
+
+**Context:** Per the project's zero-tolerance external API policy, no test or local dev run may make a real call to an external API.
+
+**Status:** PASS — This story introduces zero new external API calls. All data is sourced from the internal `/healthz` endpoint and `loader_health` / `loader_run_history` tables. The single POST (`reset-circuit`) targets an internal API route. No outbound HTTP mocking is required beyond what already exists.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Authentication & Authorization
+
+**Pattern:** The Loaders page is gated behind `PermissionGuard` with admin role requirement. The reset-circuit POST endpoint requires admin authentication via the existing Bearer token flow (Azure AD JWT or valid API key).
+
+**Status:** PASS — Follows established dashboard auth patterns. Non-admin users cannot view the page or invoke the reset action.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Input Validation
+
+- **Reset reason field:** Required, non-empty string. Submitted as JSON `{ "reason": "..." }` payload.
+- **Loader name in URL path:** Used as a path parameter for `/api/loaders/{name}/reset-circuit`. The backend validates against the registered loader names in `loaders_registry`.
+
+**Status:** PASS — No SQL injection vectors (parameterized queries), no XSS vectors (React escapes by default), no path traversal (name validated against registry).
+
+---
+
+## 5. Data Exposure
+
+The dashboard displays: loader name, health color, circuit state, consecutive failures, staleness seconds, last success timestamp, and rows loaded today. All of this data is already exposed via the `/healthz` endpoint which is admin-gated.
+
+**Status:** PASS — No new data exposure beyond existing `/healthz`.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Findings
+
+| # | Severity | Finding | Status |
+|---|----------|---------|--------|
+| 1 | Info | 30-second polling interval is reasonable; no rate-limit concern for internal `/healthz` | Accepted |
+| 2 | Info | Reset modal requires reason text — good audit trail practice | Accepted |
+
+---
+
+## 7. Conclusion
+
+No must-fix items. The story is approved for Phase 8 implementation. The feature is read-heavy, admin-gated, and follows all established security patterns.
